    <title lang="fr">Travel Thru History</title>
    <sub-title lang="fr">Oslo</sub-title>
    <desc lang="fr">We set sail to the land of the Norseman in Oslo, Norway. We'll climb the fort walls at Akershus Fortress and discover the North and South Poles at the Fram Museum. Then, we'll unearth ancient viking ship treasures at the Viking Ship Museum, and we'll brave the open waters of the Pacific with Thor Heyerdahl at the Kon-tiki museum.</desc>
    <category lang="fr">Documentaire de société</category>
    <icon src="http://static-cdn.tv.sfr.net/data/img/pl/2/7/4/15270472.jpg" />
    <episode-num system="onscreen">S3 E3</episode-num>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="DocuBox.HD.fr" start="20261105075000 +0000" stop="20261105082000 +0000">
    <title lang="fr">Nature's Force</title>
    <desc lang="fr">Weather is universal and it's also Extra Terrestrial. Learn about space weather and how it can impact us on earth. Supercells are unique storms that scientists have learnt to measure into three types. Under the earth's crust, nature is extremely energetic, and we see this through the Volcano which acts as our eye into the forces beneath our feet. Learn about the purple buzzing glow called St Elmo's Fire, how it was named and were to look for it.</desc>
    <category lang="fr">Documentaire</category>
    <icon src="http://static-cdn.tv.sfr.net/data/img/pl/4/4/9/15271944.jpg" />
    <episode-num system="onscreen">S1 E7</episode-num>
  </programme>
  
