    <title>Oddly Satisfying Science S1 - "Explosive Elements"</title>
    <desc>This week's experiments include recreating a big bang with lithium, the incendiary power of methane, and how a little bit of liquified nitrogen can lend a lot of power to a rocket.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261103062918 +0000" stop="20261103065847 +0000">
    <title>Oddly Satisfying Science S1 - "Colorful Conundrums"</title>
    <desc>This week's experiments highlight how electricity can tint titanium, how you can create a color wheel by lighting things on fire, and why the world gets all its colors from white light.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261103065847 +0000" stop="20261103072834 +0000">
    <title>Oddly Satisfying Science S1 - "Don't Believe Your Eyes"</title>
    <desc>This week's experiments delve into the possibilities of mind control, why objects and people tend to sync together, and the magical mysteries behind magnesium.</desc>
  </programme>
  
