    <title>Oddly Satisfying Science S1 - "The Sound of Science"</title>
    <desc>This week's experiments hit high notes as we discover the physics of theremins, investigate how the outer ear impacts human hearing, and put on a laser show with cymatics.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261103075840 +0000" stop="20261103081136 +0000">
    <title>Bright Now S1 - "Asteroid or Alien Tech?"</title>
    <desc>It was discovered on October 19th, 2017 and it was recognized as the first known object of its type. It is unique since it is the first known object that came from our solar system. But while we observed it, the mystery surrounding it grew.</desc>
  </programme>
  
